Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:06.00,Default,,0,0,0,,There were mothers who never crossed a classroom door, nor held a book or pen.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.00,0:00:12.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet they, more than anyone, understood that education is the truest light.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.00,0:00:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Rising before dawn, their hands grew weathered so their children could have a better tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.50,0:00:25.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Their toil was silent, passing forward the opportunities they were never given.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.00,0:00:32.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Standing outside the school gate, their deepest prayer was for us to walk inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.00,0:00:38.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Though they could not read the letters in our books...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.50,0:00:45.50,Default,,0,0,0,,...they knew one unshakable truth: learning was our only way through.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.50,0:00:52.00,Default,,0,0,0,,With hot tea by lamplight and a mother's blessing—"be strong, my child"—they gave us strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.00,0:00:58.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The achievements we celebrate today are the harvest of their prayers and sacrifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.00,0:01:05.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Every door we open carries the enduring imprint of their sweat and tears.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.00,0:01:11.00,Default,,0,0,0,,They never called themselves teachers, yet they were our first and greatest guides.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.00,0:01:17.00,Default,,0,0,0,,And the wisdom of our mothers will live on, honored through every generation.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.00,0:01:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Made with AI • Dedicated to our mothers • የእናቶቻችን ጥበብ
